General:
  UUID: "89e6bdca-7165-427e-8887-c3264fa243f1"
  Author: "sliptonic"
  License: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  Name: "POM Homopolymer"
  Description: >-
    Polyoxymethylene homopolymer (acetal homopolymer, trade name Delrin).
    Engineering thermoplastic used in precision parts requiring high stiffness,
    low friction, and excellent dimensional stability.
    Physical and mechanical properties (density, modulus, strength, thermal
    conductivity, specific heat, expansion): Wikipedia article
    "Polyoxymethylene" (CC-BY-SA-4.0), accessed 2026-02.
    NOTE: FreeCAD core's POM-Homopolymer-Generic.FCMat has a specific heat
    value of 3010 J/kg/K which is approximately double the correct value;
    the Wikipedia value of 1500 J/kg/K is used here as it matches published
    DuPont datasheets and is consistent with thermoplastic class norms.
    Machinability values are conservative defaults based on widely-published
    engineering consensus for acetal POM (one of the easiest plastics to
    machine). FreeCAD core has no machining prototype for POM. Specific
    machine/tool/setup may permit substantially higher surface speeds.
  SourceURL: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyoxymethylene"
  Tags:
    - "Plastic"
    - "Thermoplastic"
    - "POM"
    - "Acetal"
    - "Delrin"
    - "Homopolymer"
